#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This Procedure demonstrates an Event-driven test meant to simulate the application of a handbrake combined with a reverse spin maneuver. Full throttle is maintained throughout the simulation.
#
#VS Commands are used to set up the run and control the brakes, including brake system dynamics. The handbrake is applied to the rear wheels only, and its operation does not cause the brake lights to illuminate.
#
#Click on the blue link "Handbrake Turn Variable Definitions" for more information on the VS Commands.
#
#Click on the Events dataset "A. Accelerate to Speed" to learn how this example was put together.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

